within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C09C_AngiotensinIiReceptorBlockersArbsPlain.C09CA10_Fimasartan;
model Fimasartan_Kim2017_PD_dbp
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Kim_2017 :: DBP (Diastolic blood pressure)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.IndirectTurnoverSweep(
    E0 = 82.3,      // [mmHg]
    Emax = 33.8,  // type IV effect term
    EC50 = 4.82e-06,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // emax_not_a_fraction: type I needs Imax ≤ 1 but the record has 33.8; bound as the reciprocal stimulation form (IV) the paper fitted
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 7.3, Interval = 0.0146),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Fimasartan_Kim2017_PD_dbp</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Kim CO et al., <i>Translational and clinical pharmacology 25(1):43–51</i> 2017 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.12793/tcp.2017.25.1.43\">doi:10.12793/tcp.2017.25.1.43</a>) — Diastolic blood pressure [mmHg] against fimasartan ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       82.3 mmHg     drug-free response (baseline) (Base, Q324)
  Emax  =       33.8          maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =       4.82 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50,H+A, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.IndirectTurnoverSweep\">IndirectTurnoverSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of fimasartan per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><p>The effect term enters as a reciprocal (steady state of <code>der(R) = Kin - Kout*(1 + Emax*frac)*R</code>), so EC50 is the exposure at half the maximal STIMULATION of turnover, not at half the response.</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 82.3   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (4.82 ng/mL)  response 4.598
  exposure -> infinity  response 2.365</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Kim_2017: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Fimasartan_Kim2017_PD_dbp;
